    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d825">

                <pb facs="1027" n="917" xml:id="pg917"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003/782</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawes</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-06">October 6, 1931</date>.<lb/>[Received October
                        14.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2297</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Department’s instruction No. 852, July 14, 1931,<anchor n="5" xml:id="d825-f1"/>
                    relating to the proposed new treaty on extraterritorial rights of the United
                    States in China, and to state that the memorandum forwarded therewith<anchor
                        n="6" xml:id="d825-f2"/> was duly delivered to the Foreign Office. There is
                    attached hereto a copy of a memorandum in reply prepared by the Foreign Office,
                    dated October 5, 1931,<anchor n="5" xml:id="d825-f3"/> which was handed to a
                    member of the Embassy staff without comment.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>(For the Ambassador)<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ray
                            Atherton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
